    "--granularity",
    "row"
   ],
   "numerics": "log2-extended",
   "tolerance": {
    "meta.q_given_task_entropy_ratio": 4e-16
   },
   "note": "meta.q_given_task_entropy_ratio sums 3,628 p*log2(p) terms (3,623 conditional, 5 marginal), and which log2 runs depends on numpy's SIMD dispatch and the libm: one that rounds them otherwise (here: 206 conditional and 4 marginal terms, one ulp each) writes 0.9368617343176477 for the locked 0.936861734317648, every other byte identical. The generator evaluates log2 in long double (axis.signals.numerics.log2_extended), which gives the locked float; where long double is plain double the declared tolerance (about 3 ulp) names the difference"
  },
